y5-compositor for Debian / Ubuntu
=================================

Installation
------------

  sudo apt install y5-compositor

First-time configuration
------------------------

The compositor requires a complete settings file before it starts:

  y5.compositor.settings

This creates ~/.config/y5.compositor/settings.json. The session wrapper refuses
to launch without it.

Starting a session
------------------

Log out of your current session and pick **Y5 Compositor** from your display
manager's session menu.

Alternatively, from an existing graphical session:

  systemctl --user enable --now y5.service

Optional components
-------------------

These user services are installed system-wide under /usr/lib/systemd/user/:

  systemctl --user enable --now y5-polkit-agent.service
  systemctl --user enable --now xwayland.service
  systemctl --user enable --now mx-gesture-daemon.service

MX Master gesture daemon
------------------------

Copy the example config and adjust actions for your desktop:

  mkdir -p ~/.config/mx-gesture-daemon
  cp /usr/share/y5-compositor/mx-gesture-daemon/config.example.toml \
     ~/.config/mx-gesture-daemon/config.toml

Add your user to the plugdev group if udev access is required:

  sudo usermod -aG plugdev "$USER"

Developer log viewer
--------------------

Launch y5.compositor.monitor from the application menu or a terminal.

Build from source
-----------------

  sudo apt install devscripts debhelper build-essential equivs
  sudo mk-build-deps -i -r debian/control
  debuild -us -uc -b
